ogram_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"type\": \"metric\",\n  \"value\": 1.003386466259221\n },\n \"result.top_program_02\": {\n  \"attempt_id\": \"c01_min_boost_cost_by_aggregation_attempt_01\",\n  \"id\": \"result.top_program_02\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c01_min_boost_cost_by_aggregation\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/investigation/ideas/01_minimal_targeted_boost_cost_to_rank_first_across_aggregation_rules/program_1\",\n  \"program_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"type\": \"metric\",\n  \"value\": 1.0018272960697132\n },\n \"result.top_program_03\": {\n  \"attempt_id\": \"c02_milp_level_selection_solvers_attempt_01\",\n  \"id\": \"result.top_program_03\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c02_milp_level_selection_solvers\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/investigation/ideas/02_exact_milp_level_selection_solvers_for_combinatorial_aggregation_rules/program_1\",\n  \"program_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"type\": \"metric\",\n  \"value\": 1.0018272960697132\n },\n \"result.total_attempts\": {\n  \"id\": \"result.total_attempts\",\n  \"type\": \"count\",\n  \"value\": 3\n },\n \"result.total_correct_programs\": {\n  \"id\": \"result.total_correct_programs\",\n  \"type\": \"count\",\n  \"value\": 3\n },\n \"result.total_evaluated_programs\": {\n  \"id\": \"result.total_evaluated_programs\",\n  \"type\": \"count\",\n  \"value\": 3\n },\n \"result.total_ideas\": {\n  \"id\": \"result.total_ideas\",\n  \"type\": \"count\",\n  \"value\": 3\n }\n}\n== evidence_sources\n{\n \"ablations\": {\n  \"path\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/ablations\",\n  \"status\": \"missing\"\n },\n \"investigation\": {\n  \"path\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/investigation\",\n  \"status\": \"included\"\n }\n}\n== totals\n{\n \"attempts\": 3,\n \"correct_programs\": 3,\n \"evaluated_programs\": 3,\n \"ideas\": 3\n}\n== presentation_contract\n{\n \"forbidden_visible_terms\": [\n  \"eligible\",\n  \"correct and eligible\",\n  \"correctness rate\",\n  \"worker_01\",\n  \"worker_02\",\n  \"combined_score\",\n  \"rubric\"\n ],\n \"internal_fields\": [\n  \"correct\",\n  \"eligible\"\n ],\n \"preferred_terms\": {\n  \"idea\": \"model variant\",\n  \"ideas\": \"model variants\",\n  \"implementation\": \"configuration\",\n  \"implementations\": \"configurations\",\n  \"program\": \"seeded run\",\n  \"programs\": \"seeded runs\"\n },\n \"run_unit\": \"seeded_run\",\n \"threshold_rate_rule\": \"If a thresholded rate appears in the visible paper, keep one reader-facing meaning per figure, such as target attainment, successful-run fraction, or non-collapse rate. Do not reuse a single label for different task-specific thresholds.\",\n \"variant_unit\": \"model_variant\"\n}\n== improvement_trace\n[\n {\n  \"attempt_id\": \"c01_min_boost_cost_by_aggregation_attempt_01\",\n  \"combined_score\": 1.0018272960697132,\n  \"id\": \"result.improvement_001\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c01_min_boost_cost_by_aggregation\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/investigation/ideas/01_minimal_targeted_boost_cost_to_rank_first_across_aggregation_rules/program_1\",\n  \"program_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"program_idx\": 1,\n  \"step_index\": 1,\n  \"x_index\": 0\n },\n {\n  \"attempt_id\": \"c03_verified_boundary_polishing_attempt_01\",\n  \"combined_score\": 1.003386466259221,\n  \"id\": \"result.improvement_002\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c03_verified_boundary_polishing\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/a01/claude/20261111_071545/investigation/ideas/03_verified_boundary_polishing_and_transfer_local_search_for_boost_plans/program_1\",\n  \"program_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"program_idx\": 1,\n  \"step_index\": 3,\n  \"x_index\": 2\n }\n]\n== idea_titles\n[\n \"Minimal Targeted-Boost Cost to Rank First Across Aggregation Rules\",\n \"Exact MILP Level-Selection Solvers for Combinatorial Aggregation Rules\",\n \"Verified Boundary Polishing and Transfer Local Search for Boost Plans\"\n]\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 1,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_plan\": {\n    \"purpose\": \"Provide reimplementation-level detail and the full retained metric tables so the main text can stay focused on the qualified-final claim and its limits without hiding any evidence central to the thesis.\",\n    \"planned_subsections\": [\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Investment model, field construction, targets and rule definitions\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Formal definitions from the task contract: independent per-task non-negative gains, no spillover, L1 cost with cap at 100, L0 cost with each task lifted at most to the field-best, field = top-K (K = min(N,200)) fully observed models by arithmetic mean, targets at mean-rank 2 and 10, strict-first success with ties against the target; rules mean, median, 20% trimmed mean, z-score mean, Borda, plurality, Copeland, maximin.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.status\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Efficiency metric, evaluator protocol and full metric tables\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Episode efficiency = min(2, ref cost / verified plan cost) with 0.01 cost floor, 1 for correct infeasible or empty plan, 0 for failures; main = mean over boards, cases, seeds; control = mean of permuted-input and shuffled-null efficiency; combined = 0.8 main + 0.2 control; qualification rule (main > baseline and replay reproduces). Tables of final metrics, per-seed episode scores and durations (31.4 s, 33.0 s), and search metrics for three variants (episode durations 9-37 s).\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.main_efficiency\", \"final.metric.control_efficiency\", \"final.metric.baseline_main_efficiency\", \"final.metric.plan_validity_rate\", \"final.evidence.episodes\", \"result.best_correct_score\", \"result.total_attempts\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Planner components and verification procedure\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Description of per-rule solvers (exact for mean/median/maximin/plurality; verified heuristics or MILP level selection for trimmed/Borda/Copeland/z-score), exact-replica verification, pruning and fallback, and the boundary-polish stage (bisect shrink, drop redundant, pairwise transfer), taken from the retained program source.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"result.improvement_001\", \"result.improvement_002\", \"result.top_program_03\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Data provenance, snapshots and reproducibility checklist\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"HELM MMLU v1.13.0 for search; Open LLM Leaderboard contents (sha 9c09a7ca..., 2025-03-20) and results (sha aa81ecc3..., 2025-03-15) for final; evaluator, program-tree and results-tree SHA-256 values from the final manifest; seeds 9001/9002 (final) and 11/12 (search); CPU-only runtime; license caveats; LLM usage statement.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.outcome\", \"final.qualification.correct\"]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"forbidden_headings\": [\n    \"Experiment 1 / Experiment 2\",\n    \"Search Progression\",\n    \"Milestones\",\n    \"First Valid Result\",\n    \"Campaign Phases\",\n    \"Iteration History\",\n    \"What We Tried\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden_phrases\": [\n    \"correctness rate\",\n    \"correct and eligible\",\n    \"combined_score\",\n    \"rubric\",\n    \"worker_01\",\n    \"state of the art\",\n    \"proves that the leaderboard is robust\",\n    \"we trained\",\n    \"optimal planner\",\n    \"in the first attempt\",\n    \"the agent discovered\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_writer\": [\n    \"Qualification: final.qualification.outcome = qualified, status = completed, correct = true. State this plainly and remind readers that qualification means main efficiency exceeded the naive baseline and integrity checks passed; it does not certify generalization beyond the final boards or real training effects.\",\n    \"Do not present per-rule required-investment numbers, rule-ranking claims, correlation-vs-shuffled-null results, or infeasibility counts: none are in paper_data. Frame the rule-dependence question as the motivating, still-open hypothesis and state that the retained evidence addresses planner cost-efficiency only. Missing diagnostics are unknown, not negative.\",\n    \"Efficiency >1 means plans were on average slightly cheaper than the reference solver's cost; per-episode efficiency is capped at 2. Do not describe the reference as optimal, and do not call the planner optimal. Differences between variants are in the third decimal with 2 seeds; do not call them significant. Seed-level spread is the only uncertainty reported (final combined 1.00260 / 1.00257; search c03 1.00339 / 1.00339 within about 2e-5).\",\n    \"candidate_diagnostics_trust is 'unverified' for all evaluations: note that retained control and validity diagnostics come from evaluator-side recomputation but candidate-reported diagnostics were not independently verified.\",\n    \"Keep search and final strictly separate: search = HELM MMLU v1.13.0 (3 scored attempts, 0 unscored, 3 configuration variants); final = sealed Open LLM Leaderboard boards. Do not claim an improvement over a baseline in the search stage (no search baseline metric is retained).\",\n    \"Use reader-facing terms: 'model variant' or 'configuration', 'seeded run'; call the metric 'efficiency relative to the reference solver' and 'plan validity rate'. If a threshold-based rate is needed, call it 'plan validity rate' only (fraction of episodes with a well-formed in-bounds response).\",\n    \"Page budget (ICLR, 8-9 body pages, no padding): spend space on (i) a rigorous problem formalization and investment-model justification with limitations (spillover, heterogeneous cost, field size K, cap policy), (ii) the rule set and why each rule is more or less sensitive to targeted gains in principle (mark as conceptual, not measured), (iii) planner and verification design, (iv) evaluation protocol including controls and qualification rule, (v) results, and (vi) a candid limitations section. If the grounded content cannot honestly fill 8 pages, shorten the claims rather than add filler.\",\n    \"References: references.bib currently holds only three on-topic voting-manipulation entries (Dey 2014, Yang 2014, Obraztsova 2011); the remaining entries are off-topic robust-statistics papers and must not be cited for support. Starter-literature items (MMLU, HELM, Benchmark Lottery, social-choice evaluation, Leaderboard Illusion, contamination work, Handbook of Computational Social Choice) are not in references.bib; cite them only if added to the bib with verified provenance, otherwise do not cite. Do not mention or search for the withheld prior paper.\",\n    \"Overview figure uses generate-concept-figure; other figures use matplotlib exporting PDF and PNG (300 DPI) from source, with the PDF referenced from LaTeX. If raster-only, at least 2400 px wide for full-width placement. Never upscale rasters.\",\n    \"Double-blind: no author names, repositories or self-identifying links; include an LLM Usage section (may be in appendix). Include the ICLR reproducibility/ethics statements as the template requires.\",\n    \"Title should name the mechanism and setting (verified minimal-investment planning, aggregation rules, public leaderboards) and must not imply a rule-ranking or superiority result.\"\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
