{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvsWKyCNNQAErmoSz9Tk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WQrGPmd4HorzsVjxWLhDYc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\nadd = r\"\"\"\\paragraph{What a rule-dependence test would require.} Answering the motivating question needs paired, per-case costs rather than efficiencies: for each board, target rank and cost measure, the reference (or planner) cost under every rule, including infeasible cases as censored outcomes rather than zeros. Rule effects would then be summarized with bootstrap intervals over targets and compared with paired rank tests with multiplicity correction; the shuffled-score null would indicate how much of any difference comes from the correlation structure of real task scores rather than from the rule itself; and sensitivity to the field size, the cap policy and the target rank would be reported as robustness checks. The planner source contains offline helpers for the interval and test computations, but none of them was run to produce a reported number.\n\n\\paragraph{Coupling between planner and evaluator.} The planner's internal rule replica implements the same definitions that the task specifies and that the evaluator's rule engine uses, so agreement between the two on whether a plan succeeds is by construction; the evaluator nevertheless recomputes every plan with its own independent code, and a disagreement would have scored zero. The retained evidence does not report any such disagreement, but it also does not break out failure counts, other than the plan validity rate of 1.0, which only covers well-formedness.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"\\\\paragraph{Dual use.}\", add+\"\\\\paragraph{Dual use.}\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\n(pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l1.log; bibtex paper >/tmp/b.log; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l2.log; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l3.log); grep -n \"Error\\|undefined\" /tmp/l3.log | head; $TMPDIR/pyenv/bin/python - <<'E' 2>/dev/null\nimport pymupdf\nd=pymupdf.open('/workspace/paper/paper.pdf'); print(len(d))\nfor n in (8,9,10):\n    p=d[n-1]; bl=[b for b in p.get_text('blocks') if b[3]<740 and 'Generated by' not in b[4]]\n    print(n,p.get_text()[40:90].replace('\\n',' '), round(max(b[3] for b in bl)))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":171738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57f4b59f-be00-4dc5-8dc7-5e94dca033fb","uuid":"b5e0c11d-e4f6-41fa-b55d-6796402bff06","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:03:57.148Z","request_id":"req_011CgvsWJUQYyV66SAGWsrAR"}
