{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QEvQuPTqkH1doMV6QBwEkA","type":"tool_result","content":"284:The evaluated source has three layers. (i) \\emph{Exact replica.} \\texttt{verify\\_ranks\\_first} re-applies the gains to the target row and recomputes the rule on the full matrix; a margin of $2\\times10^{-8}$ is demanded locally, above the evaluator's $10^{-9}$. (ii) \\emph{Candidates.} Per-rule solvers, plus the starter uniform plan, are verified, pruned and sorted by cost. (iii) \\emph{Polish.} Up to six passes of shrink, drop and pairwise-transfer moves are applied within 2\\,s, and the result is accepted only if verified and not costlier. The MILP variant, evaluated on the development leaderboard only, adds a level-selection integer program (with a 4\\,s solver budget per episode) whose plan is accepted only after verification, so it can only tie or improve on the heuristic plan; the retained scores are identical to Base. Implementation details come from the included source files \\texttt{source\\_evidence/planner\\_boundary\\_polish\\_program.py}, \\texttt{planner\\_milp\\_variant\\_program.py} and \\texttt{planner\\_base\\_program.py}.\n289:\\paragraph{Software and runs.} Python with NumPy 2.5.4, SciPy 1.18.1 and PyArrow 26.0.1, CPU only. Development seeds 11, 12; held-out seeds 9001, 9002. Per-seed held-out evaluator wall-clock was 31.4 and 33.0\\,s. Held-out outcome identifiers: evaluator SHA-256 \\texttt{02531dad\\ldots e163e}, planner source tree \\texttt{db5d072f\\ldots d4734f} (hashes identify provenance and are not evidence of correctness). The figure script \\texttt{scripts/build\\_figures.py} regenerates Figures~\\ref{fig:final} and~\\ref{fig:search}; Tables~\\ref{tab:final} and~\\ref{tab:search} are transcriptions of retained metric files.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57f4b59f-be00-4dc5-8dc7-5e94dca033fb","uuid":"9b16d73a-5712-434a-91dd-5e21cca5535e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:04:40.718Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"284:The evaluated source has three layers. (i) \\emph{Exact replica.} \\texttt{verify\\_ranks\\_first} re-applies the gains to the target row and recomputes the rule on the full matrix; a margin of $2\\times10^{-8}$ is demanded locally, above the evaluator's $10^{-9}$. (ii) \\emph{Candidates.} Per-rule solvers, plus the starter uniform plan, are verified, pruned and sorted by cost. (iii) \\emph{Polish.} Up to six passes of shrink, drop and pairwise-transfer moves are applied within 2\\,s, and the result is accepted only if verified and not costlier. The MILP variant, evaluated on the development leaderboard only, adds a level-selection integer program (with a 4\\,s solver budget per episode) whose plan is accepted only after verification, so it can only tie or improve on the heuristic plan; the retained scores are identical to Base. Implementation details come from the included source files \\texttt{source\\_evidence/planner\\_boundary\\_polish\\_program.py}, \\texttt{planner\\_milp\\_variant\\_program.py} and \\texttt{planner\\_base\\_program.py}.\n289:\\paragraph{Software and runs.} Python with NumPy 2.5.4, SciPy 1.18.1 and PyArrow 26.0.1, CPU only. Development seeds 11, 12; held-out seeds 9001, 9002. Per-seed held-out evaluator wall-clock was 31.4 and 33.0\\,s. Held-out outcome identifiers: evaluator SHA-256 \\texttt{02531dad\\ldots e163e}, planner source tree \\texttt{db5d072f\\ldots d4734f} (hashes identify provenance and are not evidence of correctness). The figure script \\texttt{scripts/build\\_figures.py} regenerates Figures~\\ref{fig:final} and~\\ref{fig:search}; Tables~\\ref{tab:final} and~\\ref{tab:search} are transcriptions of retained metric files.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
